    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAs">VI As</ref> 1.5</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">⁊ se þe þeof wrecan wille ⁊ ǽhlip gewryce oððe on stræte togeliht, beo CXX scll. scildig wið þone cing. Gif he þonne mann ofslea on þa wrace, beo hé his feores scyldig ⁊ ealles þæs þe he áge, buton se cing him arian wille.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">And he who wishes to avenge a thief and has recourse to violence, or comes to his aid on the high road, shall forfeit 120 shillings to the king. If, however, he slays anyone in the act of vengeance, he shall forfeit his life and all he possesses, unless the king is willing to pardon him.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Et qui furem uindicare uelit et euocacionem faciet uel ad eum liberandum in uia descendet, CXX sol. reus sit apud (erga) regem. Si hominem occidat in ea þrace (uindicta), de uita forisfactus sit et de omnibus que habebit, nisi rex ei uelit misereri.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
